---
// cbf-crs-commitment-documents — the "Commitment Documents" section of the
// legacy CBFish Commitment Summary detail page, lift-and-shifted for ONE
// commitment record. Lists the due dates and documents attached to that
// specific commitment, and — unlike the read-only cross-commitment Document
// Library (cbf-crs-documents-grid.astro) — lets a user add/edit/delete them.
//
// Checked live against qa.cbfish.org/BiologicalOpinionCommitment.mvc/
// CommitmentSummary/<id>: prod renders this as a genuine interactive grid
// (sortable columns, quick search, CSV export — a legacy dhtmlxgrid widget),
// not a static list, so this is AG Grid (wireDataGrid from
// ../shared/grid-chrome), matching cbf-crs-documents-grid.astro's own
// conventions rather than the plain <table> an earlier pass built before this
// comparison was made. Our CrsDocument data model unifies a due date and its
// document into one record (a row can carry a dueDate with no filename,
// meaning "pending" — see src/data/crs-commitments.mjs), so Add Discrete Due
// Date, Upload Commitment Document, and a row's Edit action all share ONE
// dialog (cbf-crs-document-dialog.astro); Add Recurring Due Date is genuinely
// different (first date + repeat-every-N-years) and gets its own
// (cbf-crs-recurring-due-date-dialog.astro).
//
// Deleting a row that carries BOTH a dueDate and a filename (a due date
// that's already been satisfied) only clears the document, reverting the row
// to pending — the due date itself is not removed, matching prod. Only a row
// with no filename (a bare due date) or a filename with no dueDate (a
// standalone upload) has nothing left to keep, so that delete removes the
// whole row. Deleting a satisfied due date's row entirely is therefore two
// steps: delete the document, then delete the now-pending row.
//
// A commitment can only have ONE active recurring due date at a time —
// confirmed live on two commitments (one with an active rule, one without):
// prod never exposes recurring-rule editing from the per-row menu, only from
// dedicated Modify/Delete actions above the grid ("This CRS Commitment has a
// recurring due date starting at X for every N years…"). This spoke folds
// that into the single button row every due-date action lives in (Add
// Discrete Due Date / Add Recurring Due Date ⟷ Modify/Delete Recurring Due
// Date / Upload Commitment Document), with the schedule itself as plain
// status text above it — see renderRecurringBanner(). Rows the rule
// generated carry `isRecurring: true` (no group id needed — there's only
// ever one rule to reference). Modifying the rule regenerates every
// not-yet-satisfied occurrence; deleting it removes every not-yet-satisfied
// occurrence and leaves any satisfied one in place, untagged (the rule it
// belonged to no longer exists) — same "never touch a satisfied row"
// precedent as the row-level delete.
//
// An individual recurring occurrence has no per-row Delete unless it's
// already satisfied (a document attached) — an unsatisfied occurrence's due
// date can only go away via "Delete recurring due date" above, which
// correctly accounts for the whole series; deleting one row at a time would
// leave the series' own understanding of its occurrences out of sync. A
// satisfied occurrence keeps Delete because that action only ever clears the
// document (never the due date) regardless of whether the row is recurring.
//
// Edit is removed for EVERY recurring occurrence, satisfied or not — unlike
// Delete, it directly changes the date/title/category, so there's no safe
// carve-out. Only "Modify recurring due date" can change those fields, for
// the whole series at once. Upload still appears on an unsatisfied
// occurrence (attaching a file doesn't touch the series), so a document can
// still be attached without going through Edit.
//
// A commitment can only use ONE due-date scheme at a time: discrete due
// dates OR a recurring rule, never both. updateDueDateModeLocks() disables
// "Add discrete due date" while a recurring rule is active, and disables
// "Add recurring due date" while any discrete due date exists, recomputed
// after every mutation. This only gates NEW additions going forward — it
// doesn't retroactively touch pre-existing seed data that might already mix
// both. A standalone document upload (no dueDate at all) isn't part of
// either scheme and always stays available.
//
// Row actions are plain EsaIconButtons in an Actions column, not a popover —
// checked every AG Grid instance in this repo and none mounts a
// popover/dropdown-menu inside a cell; AG Grid's cell area clips
// absolutely-positioned content that doesn't portal outside it, and nothing
// here has tested that. Every existing grid instead drives actions from
// outside the cell (header button, row-click, toolbar bulk-action); plain
// icon buttons sidestep the risk entirely. Real esa-icon-button legos,
// server-rendered once in a hidden template and cloned into each row's
// Actions cell — same "clone the real lego" technique
// cbf-crs-commitment-timeline.astro uses for its status pills.
//
// Because sorting is now real (AG Grid's own column sort), a numeric array
// index is no longer a stable row identifier — editing/deleting tracks the
// row OBJECT itself, recovering its position in the backing array via
// indexOf only at the point of mutation, and every save mutates that object
// IN PLACE (never replaces it) so gridApi.applyTransaction's default
// reference-identity matching (no getRowId configured) keeps working and any
// row-tagging field (isRecurring) survives an edit automatically.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: ecology has NO table/grid lego (checked the full
// catalog). AG Grid is the same explicit dependency
// cbf-crs-documents-grid.astro already chose for sort/quick-search/CSV export
// over a hand-rolled <table>; this component follows that precedent now that
// the real reference page confirms it. Every other control is a lego:
// esa-card (section chrome), esa-empty-state (zero-rows branch), esa-button
// (header/banner actions), esa-icon-button (row actions + CSV download),
// esa-confirm-dialog (delete confirmations, same lego
// cbf-baselines-upload.astro uses for its destructive action).
import EsaCard from '@esa/ecology/esa-card.astro';
import EsaEmptyState from '@esa/ecology/esa-empty-state.astro';
import EsaButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';
import EsaIconButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-icon-button.astro';
import CbfCrsDocumentDialog from './cbf-crs-document-dialog.astro';
import CbfCrsRecurringDueDateDialog from './cbf-crs-recurring-due-date-dialog.astro';

interface CrsDocument {
  commitmentNumber: string; dueDate?: string; category: string; type: string;
  title: string; description: string; filename?: string; uploadDate?: string; uploadUser?: string;
}
interface Props {
  documents?: CrsDocument[];
  commitmentNumber: string;
  commitmentEndDate: string;
}
const { documents = [], commitmentNumber, commitmentEndDate } = Astro.props;
const hasDocuments = documents.length > 0;
---
<EsaCard title="Commitment documents">
  <div class="cbf-crs-commitment-documents__empty" data-crs-doc-empty hidden={hasDocuments}>
    <EsaEmptyState
      title="No due dates or documents yet"
      description="Add a discrete due date, a recurring due date, or upload a document with no due date."
    >
      <div class="cluster" data-gap="sm">
        <span data-crs-doc-add-discrete><EsaButton color="primary" icon="calendar">Add discrete due date</EsaButton></span>
        <span data-crs-doc-add-recurring><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" icon="calendar">Add recurring due date</EsaButton></span>
        <span data-crs-doc-add-upload><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" icon="upload">Upload document</EsaButton></span>
      </div>
    </EsaEmptyState>
  </div>

  <div class="cbf-crs-commitment-documents__populated stack" data-gap="md" data-crs-doc-populated hidden={!hasDocuments}>
    <p class="cbf-crs-commitment-documents__intro type-caption">
      A commitment can have discrete due dates or one recurring due date, not both. An individual
      recurring occurrence can only be edited or deleted as part of the whole series.
    </p>

    <!-- Recurring due date's schedule, shown only while a rule is active — the Add/Modify/Delete
         actions themselves live in the button row below instead, so this is status text only.
         Toggled by the client script's renderRecurringBanner() whenever recurringRule changes. -->
    <p class="type-caption" data-crs-recurring-status hidden>
      Recurring due date: starts <strong data-crs-recurring-banner-date></strong>, every
      <strong data-crs-recurring-banner-step></strong>.
    </p>

    <!-- One row for every due-date/document action. Add recurring due date and
         Modify/Delete recurring due date are mutually exclusive (toggled by
         renderRecurringBanner() — a commitment has at most one active rule, see
         header note), everything else is always available. -->
    <div class="cbf-crs-commitment-documents__toolbar cluster" data-gap="sm">
      <span data-crs-doc-add-discrete><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" icon="calendar" size="sm">Add discrete due date</EsaButton></span>
      <span data-crs-doc-add-recurring><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" icon="calendar" size="sm">Add recurring due date</EsaButton></span>
      <span data-crs-doc-modify-recurring hidden><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" size="sm">Modify recurring due date</EsaButton></span>
      <span data-crs-doc-delete-recurring hidden><EsaButton color="danger" appearance="outline" size="sm">Delete recurring due date</EsaButton></span>
      <span data-crs-doc-add-upload><EsaButton color="secondary" appearance="outline" icon="upload" size="sm">Upload document</EsaButton></span>
    </div>

    <!-- AG Grid mounts here. autoHeight grows with rows so the page (not an inner
         pane) owns vertical scroll; the wrapper owns the framed surface. -->
    <div class="cbf-crs-doc-grid" data-crs-doc-grid></div>

    <footer class="cbf-crs-commitment-documents__footer repel">
      <span class="type-caption" data-crs-doc-count>
        Showing {documents.length} of {documents.length} due dates/documents
      </span>
      <span data-crs-doc-csv><EsaIconButton icon="download" label="Download CSV" size="sm" /></span>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <!-- Real esa-icon-button legos, server-rendered once, cloned into each row's
       Actions cell — see header note on why this isn't a popover menu. -->
  <template data-crs-doc-action-templates hidden aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-action-template="edit"><EsaIconButton icon="pencil" label="Edit" size="sm" /></span>
    <span data-action-template="upload"><EsaIconButton icon="upload" label="Upload document" size="sm" /></span>
    <span data-action-template="delete"><EsaIconButton icon="trash-2" label="Delete" size="sm" /></span>
  </template>

  <CbfCrsDocumentDialog />
  <CbfCrsRecurringDueDateDialog />

  <esa-confirm-dialog
    data-crs-doc-delete-confirm
    heading="Delete this row?"
    variant="danger"
    confirm-label="Delete"
    cancel-label="Cancel"
  ></esa-confirm-dialog>

  <esa-confirm-dialog
    data-crs-recurring-delete-confirm
    heading="Delete recurring due date?"
    variant="danger"
    confirm-label="Delete"
    cancel-label="Cancel"
  ></esa-confirm-dialog>

  <!-- Row data for the grid, serialized so the client module (which imports
       ag-grid-community) hydrates without a second fetch — same convention as
       every other AG-Grid data component in this spoke. Kept as its own
       element (rather than nested in the config blob) so wireDataGrid's
       dataSelector can parse it directly into the SAME array this file's
       script mutates — no second, diverging copy of the data. -->
  <script type="application/json" data-crs-doc-rows set:html={JSON.stringify(documents)}></script>
  <script
    type="application/json"
    data-crs-doc-config
    set:html={JSON.stringify({ commitmentNumber, commitmentEndDate })}
  ></script>
</EsaCard>

<style>
  /* Same author-CSS-beats-UA-stylesheet issue cbf-password-gate.astro documents:
     the global .stack utility's unconditional `display: flex` sits later in the
     cascade than the UA stylesheet's `[hidden]{display:none}` at equal
     specificity, so it wins and the "populated" branch stays visible even with
     the hidden attribute set. Restated here with the attribute in the selector
     so it actually wins. */
  .cbf-crs-commitment-documents__populated[hidden],
  .cbf-crs-commitment-documents__empty[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .cbf-crs-commitment-documents__intro,
  [data-crs-recurring-status] {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 90ch;
  }

  .cbf-crs-doc-grid :global(.ag-root-wrapper) {
    border-radius: var(--radius-100, 4px);
  }

  .cbf-crs-commitment-documents__footer {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  /* Actions cell: a few icon buttons side by side, no popover — see header note. */
  .cbf-crs-doc-grid :global(.cbf-crs-doc-actions) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-100, 0.25rem);
  }
</style>

<script>
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-confirm-dialog';
  import {
    gridDateFormatter as dateFmt,
    asGridDate as asDate,
    wireDataGrid,
  } from '../shared/grid-chrome';
  import { toISODate, isoToUSDate } from '../../lib/dates';

  interface DocRow {
    commitmentNumber: string; dueDate?: string; category: string; type: string;
    title: string; description: string; filename?: string; uploadDate?: string; uploadUser?: string;
    // Set only on rows generated by the one active recurring rule (mock/seed
    // data predates this and never carries it) — there's at most one rule per
    // commitment, so a boolean is enough; no group id needed.
    isRecurring?: true;
  }
  // The recurring rule itself, independent of any one generated occurrence —
  // stored so "Modify recurring due date" can prefill the ORIGINAL rule
  // (title without its " — YYYY" suffix, the rule's own first date/step), not
  // something reverse-engineered from whatever rows happen to still exist.
  interface RecurringRule {
    title: string; firstDueDate: string; repeatYears: number;
    description: string; type: string; category: string;
  }
  type DocField = HTMLElement & { value?: string; required?: boolean };
  type DialogEl = HTMLElement & { show: () => void; close: () => void; heading?: string };
  type ConfirmDialogEl = HTMLElement & { open: boolean; message: string; heading: string };

  const MOCK_USER = 'Angela Zhao';
  const HORIZON_YEAR = 2035;

  // "M/D/YYYY" string -> year, without a Date object round-trip — same
  // reasoning as the recurring-generation math below (new Date() on a
  // date-only string can silently shift under local-time reads/writes).
  function yearOfUSDate(s?: string): number | null {
    if (!s) return null;
    const parts = s.split('/');
    return parts.length === 3 ? Number(parts[2]) : null;
  }

  function initDocuments(root: HTMLElement) {
    const configEl = root.querySelector<HTMLScriptElement>('[data-crs-doc-config]');
    if (!configEl) return;
    const config = JSON.parse(configEl.textContent ?? '{}') as {
      commitmentNumber: string; commitmentEndDate: string;
    };
    const commitmentNumber = config.commitmentNumber;
    const commitmentEndYear = Number(new Date(config.commitmentEndDate).getFullYear()) || HORIZON_YEAR;

    const emptyEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-empty]');
    const populatedEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-populated]');
    const actionTemplates = root.querySelector<HTMLTemplateElement>('[data-crs-doc-action-templates]');
    if (!emptyEl || !populatedEl || !actionTemplates) return;

    function actionButtonHTML(action: 'edit' | 'upload' | 'delete'): string {
      const el = actionTemplates!.content.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-action-template="${action}"]`);
      return el?.outerHTML ?? '';
    }

    // ── Document dialog (Add Discrete Due Date / Upload Document / Edit) ──
    const docDialog = root.querySelector<DialogEl>('[data-crs-doc-dialog]');
    const docForm = root.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('[data-crs-doc-form]');
    const docCancel = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-cancel]');
    const docSave = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-save]');
    const docError = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-error]');
    const docUploadedLine = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-uploaded]');
    const docUploadedName = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-uploaded-name]');
    const docFileSlot = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-file-slot]');
    const docExistingWrap = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-existing-wrap]');
    const docExistingSelect = root.querySelector<DocField>('[data-field="existingDueDate"]');

    const docField = (name: string): DocField | null =>
      docForm?.querySelector<DocField>(`[data-field="${name}"]`) ?? null;
    const docFieldValue = (name: string): string => (docField(name)?.value ?? '').trim();

    function resetDocFileUpload(): void {
      if (!docFileSlot) return;
      const old = docFileSlot.firstElementChild;
      const fresh = document.createElement('esa-file-upload');
      fresh.setAttribute('data-crs-doc-file', '');
      fresh.setAttribute('label', 'File to upload');
      fresh.setAttribute('accept', '.pdf,.doc,.docx,.xls,.xlsx');
      fresh.setAttribute('max-size-mb', '10');
      old ? old.replaceWith(fresh) : docFileSlot.appendChild(fresh);
    }

    function resetDocForm(): void {
      docForm?.querySelectorAll<DocField>('[data-field]').forEach((el) => {
        if ('value' in el) el.value = '';
      });
      if (docError) docError.hidden = true;
      if (docUploadedLine) docUploadedLine.hidden = true;
      resetDocFileUpload();
    }

    // Editing/attaching targets the row OBJECT itself, not an array index —
    // AG Grid's own column sort means display order and backing-array order
    // can diverge, so an index captured at click time could point at the
    // wrong row by the time Save runs. See this file's header note.
    let editingDoc: DocRow | null = null;
    let pendingExistingDoc: DocRow | null = null;
    let pendingFile: File | null = null;
    // Due date is required for a real due date (discrete or an existing
    // pending row), but NOT for a standalone document upload with no date —
    // this dialog is shared across both, so the requirement toggles per open
    // rather than being baked into the static markup. See openDocDialog.
    let dueDateRequired = false;

    root.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const fromDocUpload = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest?.('[data-crs-doc-file-slot]');
      if (fromDocUpload) {
        const files = (e as CustomEvent).detail?.files ?? [];
        pendingFile = files[0] ?? null;
        return;
      }
      if (e.target === docExistingSelect) {
        const raw = docExistingSelect?.value ?? '';
        pendingExistingDoc = raw === '' ? null : (existingDueDateOptionDocs[Number(raw)] ?? null);
        if (pendingExistingDoc) prefillFromDoc(pendingExistingDoc);
        else clearPrefillableFields();
      }
    });

    function prefillFromDoc(doc: DocRow): void {
      if (docField('title')) docField('title')!.value = doc.title ?? '';
      if (docField('dueDate')) docField('dueDate')!.value = toISODate(doc.dueDate) ?? '';
      if (docField('description')) docField('description')!.value = doc.description ?? '';
      if (docField('type')) docField('type')!.value = doc.type ?? '';
      if (docField('category')) docField('category')!.value = doc.category ?? '';
      if (doc.filename && docUploadedLine && docUploadedName) {
        docUploadedName.textContent = doc.filename;
        docUploadedLine.hidden = false;
      } else if (docUploadedLine) {
        docUploadedLine.hidden = true;
      }
    }

    function clearPrefillableFields(): void {
      ['title', 'dueDate', 'description', 'type', 'category'].forEach((name) => {
        if (docField(name)) docField(name)!.value = '';
      });
      if (docUploadedLine) docUploadedLine.hidden = true;
    }

    // Options are this commitment's pending due dates (a dueDate tracked, no
    // file attached yet) — exactly the rows a fresh upload could satisfy.
    // Rebuilt fresh on every open since docs can change between opens; the
    // select's value is just an index into THIS local array, not into `docs`
    // (which may be sorted differently), resolved back to the real row via
    // existingDueDateOptionDocs.
    let existingDueDateOptionDocs: DocRow[] = [];
    function populateExistingDueDateOptions(): void {
      if (!docExistingSelect) return;
      existingDueDateOptionDocs = docs.filter((doc) => doc.dueDate && !doc.filename);
      const options = existingDueDateOptionDocs.map((doc, index) => ({
        label: `${doc.title}${doc.dueDate ? ` (due ${doc.dueDate})` : ''}`,
        value: String(index),
      }));
      (docExistingSelect as unknown as { options: Array<{ label: string; value: string }> }).options = options;
    }

    function openDocDialog(
      heading: string,
      doc: DocRow | null,
      opts: { showExisting?: boolean; requireDueDate?: boolean } = {},
    ): void {
      editingDoc = doc;
      pendingExistingDoc = null;
      pendingFile = null;
      resetDocForm();
      if (docDialog) docDialog.heading = heading;
      if (docExistingWrap) docExistingWrap.hidden = !opts.showExisting;
      if (opts.showExisting) populateExistingDueDateOptions();
      if (doc) prefillFromDoc(doc);
      dueDateRequired = opts.requireDueDate ?? false;
      const dueDateField = docField('dueDate');
      if (dueDateField) dueDateField.required = dueDateRequired;
      if (docError) {
        docError.textContent = dueDateRequired
          ? 'Enter a document title and due date to continue.'
          : 'Enter a document title to continue.';
      }
      docDialog?.show();
    }

    // Each action button appears twice (empty state + populated toolbar) —
    // wire every match, not just the first. The click listener sits on the
    // OUTER wrapper span (needed since EsaButton forwards no data-* props —
    // see header note elsewhere in this spoke), so disabling only the INNER
    // native <button> via updateDueDateModeLocks() doesn't stop clicks from
    // reaching this listener; each handler re-checks the button's own
    // disabled state before acting.
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-add-discrete]').forEach((wrap) =>
      wrap.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (wrap.querySelector('button')?.disabled) return;
        openDocDialog('Add discrete due date', null, { requireDueDate: true });
      }));
    root.querySelectorAll('[data-crs-doc-add-upload]').forEach((btn) =>
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => openDocDialog('Upload commitment document', null, { showExisting: true, requireDueDate: false })));

    docCancel?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      docDialog?.close();
      editingDoc = null;
      pendingExistingDoc = null;
    });

    docSave?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const title = docFieldValue('title');
      const dueDateValue = docFieldValue('dueDate');
      if (!title || (dueDateRequired && !dueDateValue)) {
        if (docError) docError.hidden = false;
        return;
      }
      const targetDoc = editingDoc ?? pendingExistingDoc;
      const filename = pendingFile?.name ?? targetDoc?.filename;
      const uploadedNow = pendingFile != null;
      const fields = {
        title,
        dueDate: isoToUSDate(docFieldValue('dueDate')),
        description: docFieldValue('description'),
        type: docFieldValue('type'),
        category: docFieldValue('category'),
        filename,
        uploadDate: uploadedNow ? new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US') : targetDoc?.uploadDate,
        uploadUser: uploadedNow ? MOCK_USER : targetDoc?.uploadUser,
      };

      let message: string;
      if (targetDoc) {
        // Mutate in place — never replace the object — so AG Grid's
        // reference-identity `update` matching keeps working and any tag
        // (isRecurring) survives automatically. See header note.
        Object.assign(targetDoc, fields);
        gridApi.applyTransaction({ update: [targetDoc] });
        message = `${targetDoc.title} updated.`;
      } else {
        const row: DocRow = { commitmentNumber, ...fields };
        docs.unshift(row);
        gridApi.applyTransaction({ add: [row], addIndex: 0 });
        countState.total += 1;
        message = `${row.title} added.`;
      }
      syncEmptyState();
      updateDueDateModeLocks();
      toast(message);
      docDialog?.close();
      editingDoc = null;
      pendingExistingDoc = null;
    });

    // ── Recurring due date dialog — one active rule per commitment, matching
    // prod (see header note). Managed entirely from the banner above the
    // grid, never from a per-row action. ──
    const recDialog = root.querySelector<DialogEl>('[data-crs-recurring-dialog]');
    const recForm = root.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('[data-crs-recurring-form]');
    const recCancel = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-recurring-cancel]');
    const recSave = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-recurring-save]');
    const recError = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-recurring-error]');

    const recField = (name: string): DocField | null =>
      recForm?.querySelector<DocField>(`[data-field="${name}"]`) ?? null;
    const recFieldValue = (name: string): string => (recField(name)?.value ?? '').trim();

    function resetRecForm(): void {
      recForm?.querySelectorAll<DocField>('[data-field]').forEach((el) => {
        if ('value' in el) el.value = '';
      });
      if (recField('repeatYears')) recField('repeatYears')!.value = '1';
      if (recError) recError.hidden = true;
    }

    function prefillRecFromRule(rule: RecurringRule): void {
      if (recField('title')) recField('title')!.value = rule.title;
      if (recField('firstDueDate')) recField('firstDueDate')!.value = rule.firstDueDate;
      if (recField('repeatYears')) recField('repeatYears')!.value = String(rule.repeatYears);
      if (recField('description')) recField('description')!.value = rule.description;
      if (recField('type')) recField('type')!.value = rule.type;
      if (recField('category')) recField('category')!.value = rule.category;
      if (recError) recError.hidden = true;
    }

    let recurringRule: RecurringRule | null = null;

    const recurringStatus = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-recurring-status]');
    const recurringBannerDate = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-recurring-banner-date]');
    const recurringBannerStep = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-recurring-banner-step]');
    const modifyRecurringWrap = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-modify-recurring]');
    const deleteRecurringWrap = root.querySelector<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-delete-recurring]');

    // Add recurring due date vs. Modify/Delete recurring due date are
    // mutually exclusive — a commitment has at most one active rule (see
    // header note) — so exactly one of those button states is ever visible.
    // "Add recurring due date" appears twice (empty state + populated
    // toolbar, same as every other action button in this file) — Modify/
    // Delete only ever exist in the populated toolbar, since a rule can't be
    // active while the empty state (zero rows) is showing.
    function renderRecurringBanner(): void {
      const active = recurringRule != null;
      if (recurringStatus) recurringStatus.hidden = !active;
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement & { hidden: boolean }>('[data-crs-doc-add-recurring]').forEach((wrap) => {
        wrap.hidden = active;
      });
      if (modifyRecurringWrap) modifyRecurringWrap.hidden = !active;
      if (deleteRecurringWrap) deleteRecurringWrap.hidden = !active;
      if (active && recurringRule) {
        if (recurringBannerDate) recurringBannerDate.textContent = isoToUSDate(recurringRule.firstDueDate) ?? recurringRule.firstDueDate;
        if (recurringBannerStep) recurringBannerStep.textContent = `${recurringRule.repeatYears} year${recurringRule.repeatYears === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
      }
    }

    // A commitment can only use ONE due-date scheme at a time — discrete due
    // dates OR a recurring rule, never both — so each "Add" entry point
    // disables itself once the other scheme is in play. Only gates NEW
    // additions; pre-existing seed data that already mixes both (predating
    // this rule) is left alone. A standalone upload (no dueDate at all)
    // isn't part of either scheme and stays available regardless.
    //
    // EsaButton's dimmed/not-allowed look comes from an `esa-button--disabled`
    // class on its OWN wrapper span, baked in from its `disabled` prop at
    // render time — setting the native <button>'s disabled attribute alone
    // (the only thing reachable from outside after render) blocks clicks but
    // leaves it looking fully active. Toggle both.
    function setAddButtonDisabled(wrap: HTMLElement, disabled: boolean, title: string): void {
      const esaButton = wrap.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.esa-button');
      const btn = wrap.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('button');
      esaButton?.classList.toggle('esa-button--disabled', disabled);
      if (btn) {
        btn.disabled = disabled;
        btn.title = title;
      }
    }

    function updateDueDateModeLocks(): void {
      const hasDiscrete = docs.some((d) => d.dueDate && !d.isRecurring);
      const blockDiscrete = recurringRule != null;
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-add-discrete]').forEach((wrap) => {
        setAddButtonDisabled(wrap, blockDiscrete, blockDiscrete
          ? 'This commitment has an active recurring due date — delete it to add a discrete due date instead.'
          : '');
      });
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-add-recurring]').forEach((wrap) => {
        setAddButtonDisabled(wrap, hasDiscrete, hasDiscrete
          ? 'This commitment already has discrete due dates — delete them to set up a recurring due date instead.'
          : '');
      });
    }

    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-crs-doc-add-recurring]').forEach((wrap) =>
      wrap.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (wrap.querySelector('button')?.disabled) return;
        resetRecForm();
        if (recDialog) recDialog.heading = 'Add recurring due date';
        recDialog?.show();
      }));
    root.querySelector('[data-crs-doc-modify-recurring]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!recurringRule) return;
      prefillRecFromRule(recurringRule);
      if (recDialog) recDialog.heading = 'Modify recurring due date';
      recDialog?.show();
    });
    recCancel?.addEventListener('click', () => recDialog?.close());

    recSave?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const title = recFieldValue('title');
      const firstDueDate = recFieldValue('firstDueDate');
      if (!title || !firstDueDate) {
        if (recError) recError.hidden = false;
        return;
      }
      const step = Math.max(1, Number(recFieldValue('repeatYears')) || 1);
      const description = recFieldValue('description');
      const type = recFieldValue('type');
      const category = recFieldValue('category');
      const capYear = Math.min(commitmentEndYear, HORIZON_YEAR);

      // Pure calendar-component math — no Date object round-trip. firstDueDate
      // is ISO ("YYYY-MM-DD") from esa-date-picker; `new Date()` parses a
      // date-only ISO string as UTC midnight, but its getFullYear()/setFullYear()
      // read/write LOCAL time, so mutating a parsed Date's year can silently
      // shift the day in any timezone behind UTC. Working on the Y/M/D
      // components directly sidesteps that, and storing M/D/YYYY (not ISO)
      // keeps every generated row on the same local-parse path as the rest of
      // the mock dataset — see isoToUSDate's comment above.
      const [firstYear, month, day] = firstDueDate.split('-').map(Number);

      const isModify = recurringRule != null;
      recurringRule = { title, firstDueDate, repeatYears: step, description, type, category };

      // Occurrences already satisfied (a document attached) are locked — the
      // edited rule never touches them, same "delete only removes the
      // document" precedent for a single occurrence. Every OTHER occurrence
      // is discarded and regenerated fresh below, so a changed title/date/
      // step/category always applies retroactively to anything not yet
      // satisfied.
      const satisfiedYears = new Set<number>();
      const removed: DocRow[] = [];
      if (isModify) {
        for (let i = docs.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
          const d = docs[i];
          if (!d.isRecurring) continue;
          if (d.filename) {
            const y = yearOfUSDate(d.dueDate);
            if (y != null) satisfiedYears.add(y);
          } else {
            removed.push(d);
            docs.splice(i, 1);
          }
        }
      }

      const generated: DocRow[] = [];
      for (let year = firstYear; year <= capYear; year += step) {
        if (satisfiedYears.has(year)) continue;
        generated.push({
          commitmentNumber,
          title: `${title} — ${year}`,
          dueDate: `${month}/${day}/${year}`,
          description,
          type,
          category,
          isRecurring: true,
        });
      }
      docs.unshift(...generated.reverse());
      gridApi.applyTransaction({ remove: removed, add: generated, addIndex: 0 });
      countState.total += generated.length - removed.length;
      syncEmptyState();
      renderRecurringBanner();
      updateDueDateModeLocks();
      toast(isModify
        ? `${generated.length} due date${generated.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} updated.`
        : `${generated.length} due date${generated.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} added.`);
      recDialog?.close();
    });

    const recurringDeleteConfirm = root.querySelector<ConfirmDialogEl>('[data-crs-recurring-delete-confirm]');
    root.querySelector('[data-crs-doc-delete-recurring]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!recurringRule || !recurringDeleteConfirm) return;
      recurringDeleteConfirm.message = `Delete the recurring due date "${recurringRule.title}"? Any occurrence that already has a document attached will remain. This can't be undone.`;
      recurringDeleteConfirm.open = true;
    });
    recurringDeleteConfirm?.addEventListener('confirm', () => {
      const removed: DocRow[] = [];
      for (let i = docs.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        const d = docs[i];
        if (!d.isRecurring) continue;
        if (d.filename) delete d.isRecurring; // satisfied — survives, untagged
        else { removed.push(d); docs.splice(i, 1); }
      }
      gridApi.applyTransaction({ remove: removed });
      countState.total -= removed.length;
      recurringRule = null;
      syncEmptyState();
      renderRecurringBanner();
      updateDueDateModeLocks();
      toast('Recurring due date deleted.');
    });

    // ── Delete confirmation (single row) ──
    // A row with both a dueDate and a filename represents a due date that's
    // already been satisfied — matches prod: deleting it only removes the
    // uploaded document and reverts the row to "pending" (dueDate persists).
    // Only a row with no filename (a bare due date) or a filename with no
    // dueDate (a standalone upload) has nothing left to keep, so THAT delete
    // removes the whole row. To delete a satisfied due date's row entirely,
    // a user deletes the document first, then deletes the now-pending row.
    const deleteConfirm = root.querySelector<ConfirmDialogEl>('[data-crs-doc-delete-confirm]');
    let deleteDoc: DocRow | null = null;

    deleteConfirm?.addEventListener('confirm', () => {
      if (!deleteDoc) return;
      if (deleteDoc.filename && deleteDoc.dueDate) {
        deleteDoc.filename = undefined;
        deleteDoc.uploadDate = undefined;
        deleteDoc.uploadUser = undefined;
        gridApi.applyTransaction({ update: [deleteDoc] });
        toast(`Document removed from ${deleteDoc.title}.`);
      } else {
        const idx = docs.indexOf(deleteDoc);
        if (idx !== -1) docs.splice(idx, 1);
        gridApi.applyTransaction({ remove: [deleteDoc] });
        countState.total -= 1;
        syncEmptyState();
        toast(`${deleteDoc.title} deleted.`);
      }
      updateDueDateModeLocks();
      deleteDoc = null;
    });

    // ── Rendering ──
    function toast(message: string): void {
      const snackbar = document.querySelector<HTMLElement & { success?: (msg: string, cfg?: unknown) => void }>('[data-snackbar]');
      snackbar?.success?.(message, { duration: 4000 });
    }

    function syncEmptyState(): void {
      const hasDocs = docs.length > 0;
      const wasEmpty = !emptyEl!.hidden;
      emptyEl!.hidden = hasDocs;
      populatedEl!.hidden = !hasDocs;
      // AG Grid's autoHeight layout can't measure a container that started
      // out display:none — the empty→populated transition is the one moment
      // that happens, so nudge it to remeasure once visible.
      if (wasEmpty && hasDocs) requestAnimationFrame(() => gridApi.sizeColumnsToFit());
    }

    const handle = wireDataGrid<DocRow>({
      root,
      gridSelector: '[data-crs-doc-grid]',
      dataSelector: '[data-crs-doc-rows]',
      countSelector: '[data-crs-doc-count]',
      csvSelector: '[data-crs-doc-csv]',
      countNoun: 'due dates/documents',
      csvFileName: `${commitmentNumber}-documents.csv`,
      suppressCellFocus: true,
      columnDefs: [
        {
          headerName: 'Actions', colId: 'actions', minWidth: 140, width: 140, flex: 0,
          sortable: false, resizable: false,
          cellRenderer: (p: { data: DocRow }) => {
            const doc = p.data;
            // An unsatisfied recurring occurrence has no individual Delete —
            // the due date only goes away via "Delete recurring due date" in
            // the banner, which properly accounts for the whole series. A
            // SATISFIED occurrence still gets Delete: that only clears the
            // document (see the delete-confirmation note below), never the
            // due date itself, so it's unaffected by this restriction. Edit
            // has no such carve-out — it can change the date/title/category
            // directly, so it's removed for EVERY recurring occurrence
            // (satisfied or not); only "Modify recurring due date" in the
            // banner can change those fields, and only for the series as a
            // whole.
            const canDeleteRow = !doc.isRecurring || !!doc.filename;
            return [
              !doc.isRecurring ? actionButtonHTML('edit') : '',
              !doc.filename ? actionButtonHTML('upload') : '',
              canDeleteRow ? actionButtonHTML('delete') : '',
            ].join('');
          },
        },
        {
          headerName: 'Due date', field: 'dueDate', colId: 'dueDate', minWidth: 120,
          cellDataType: 'date',
          valueGetter: (p) => asDate(p.data?.dueDate),
          valueFormatter: (p) => (p.value instanceof Date ? dateFmt.format(p.value) : ''),
        },
        { headerName: 'Category', field: 'category', colId: 'category', minWidth: 200 },
        { headerName: 'Type', field: 'type', colId: 'type', minWidth: 150 },
        {
          headerName: 'Title', field: 'title', colId: 'title', flex: 2, minWidth: 220,
          getQuickFilterText: (p) => p.data?.title ?? '',
        },
        { headerName: 'Description', field: 'description', colId: 'description', flex: 3, minWidth: 260 },
        {
          headerName: 'Filename', field: 'filename', colId: 'filename', minWidth: 200,
          getQuickFilterText: (p) => p.data?.filename ?? '',
        },
        {
          headerName: 'Upload date', field: 'uploadDate', colId: 'uploadDate', minWidth: 130,
          cellDataType: 'date',
          valueGetter: (p) => asDate(p.data?.uploadDate),
          valueFormatter: (p) => (p.value instanceof Date ? dateFmt.format(p.value) : ''),
        },
        { headerName: 'Upload user', field: 'uploadUser', colId: 'uploadUser', minWidth: 150 },
      ],
      gridOptions: {
        onCellClicked: (event) => {
          if (event.column.getColId() !== 'actions') return;
          const target = (event.event as MouseEvent | null)?.target as HTMLElement | null;
          const actionEl = target?.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-action-template]');
          const action = actionEl?.dataset.actionTemplate;
          const doc = event.data as DocRow | undefined;
          if (!doc) return;
          if (action === 'edit') {
            // Belt-and-suspenders: the button is already omitted for
            // recurring rows (see the Actions cellRenderer), but guard here
            // too in case of a stale render.
            if (doc.isRecurring) return;
            openDocDialog('Edit due date / document', doc, { requireDueDate: !!doc.dueDate });
          }
          else if (action === 'upload') openDocDialog('Upload document', doc, { requireDueDate: !!doc.dueDate });
          else if (action === 'delete') {
            // Belt-and-suspenders: the button is already omitted for these
            // rows (see the Actions cellRenderer), but guard here too in
            // case of a stale render.
            if (doc.isRecurring && !doc.filename) return;
            deleteDoc = doc;
            const documentOnly = !!(doc.filename && doc.dueDate);
            if (deleteConfirm) {
              deleteConfirm.heading = documentOnly ? 'Delete this document?' : 'Delete this row?';
              deleteConfirm.message = documentOnly
                ? `Delete the uploaded document for "${doc.title}"? The due date will remain. This can't be undone.`
                : `Delete "${doc.title}"? This can't be undone.`;
              deleteConfirm.open = true;
            }
          }
        },
      },
    });
    if (!handle) return;
    const { gridApi, data: docs, countState } = handle;

    // Seed recurringRule from any rows already tagged isRecurring — none in
    // the mock/seed data today, but keeps this correct if that ever changes.
    const seededRule = docs.find((d) => d.isRecurring);
    if (seededRule) {
      recurringRule = {
        title: seededRule.title.replace(/ — \d{4}$/, ''),
        firstDueDate: toISODate(seededRule.dueDate) ?? '',
        repeatYears: 1,
        description: seededRule.description,
        type: seededRule.type,
        category: seededRule.category,
      };
    }
    renderRecurringBanner();
    updateDueDateModeLocks();
  }

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLScriptElement>('[data-crs-doc-config]')
    .forEach((configEl) => {
      const root = configEl.closest<HTMLElement>('.esa-card');
      if (root) initDocuments(root);
    });
</script>
